KV db has to manage notifications, booking requests and user session data
- NOTIFICATIONS: when a notification has to be send to a user it gets created and loaded inside the KV db; this allows a fast retrival of the notification when the user opens the application
	FORMAT: 
		- Key: user:inbox:{userId}
		- Value: list of all notifications about the specific user
	EXAMPLE:
		- key -> user:inbox:user_123
		- value ->
			[
			  {
				"msg_id": "msg_001",
				"type": "RIDE_UPDATE",
				"content": "Il driver Andrea ha accettato la tua offerta per Pisa-Bologna.",
				"timestamp": "2026-06-16T09:35:00Z",
				"read": false
			  },
			  {
				"msg_id": "msg_002",
				"type": "PAYMENT_REMINDER",
				"content": "Hai 10 minuti per completare il pagamento.",
				"timestamp": "2026-06-16T09:36:00Z",
				"read": false
			  }
			]
		
- BOOKING REQUESTS: when a user try to purchase a seat for a published ride, his request is added to the KV db and stays there until the driver accept/decline his request. If the request is accepted we update the ride document in MONGOdb with the correct number of avilable seats
	FORMAT:
		- Key: booking:req:{requestId}
		- Value: details like passenger, ride, number of seats requested, state of the booking request
		- TTL: used to manage auto-expirependig requests
	EXAMPLE:
		- key -> booking:req:BR-998877
		- value -> 
			{
			  "user_id": "user_123",
			  "ride_id": "ride_555",
			  "status": "PENDING_DRIVER_APPROVAL",
			  "seats_requested": 2,
			  "price_proposed": 15.50,
			  "created_at": "2026-06-16T09:30:00Z",
			  "expires_at": "2026-06-16T09:40:00Z"
			}
- SESSION DATA: when a user is logged in, we save his information in order to not make the user sing-in every time he wants to perform an action (examples: view profile, book a ride, see his reviews)
	FORMAT:
		- Key: session:{token}
		- Value: user details needed to not access the other databases every api we call
	EXAMPLE:
		- key -> session:token:abc-123-xyz
		- value -> 
			{
			  "user_id": "user_123",
			  "email": "johanna.doe@example.com",
			  "role": "PASSENGER",
			  "is_verified": true,
			  "last_access": "2026-06-16T10:05:00Z"
			}
